WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:02.855
The dataset is the backbone of the study.

00:00:02.935 --> 00:00:07.936
Starting from RNAInter, with over forty-seven
million RNA interactions,

00:00:08.016 --> 00:00:13.448
the authors recover sequences by cross-referencing
NCBI, UniProt and Ensembl,

00:00:13.528 --> 00:00:17.885
and assign RNA families from Rfam and protein clans
from Pfam.

00:00:17.965 --> 00:00:24.899
Those annotations let them generate negatives that
are biologically meaningful rather than random.

00:00:24.979 --> 00:00:30.983
The final RNAInterAct set holds about one hundred
twenty-two thousand interactions at

00:00:31.063 --> 00:00:33.846
a one-to-two positive-to-negative ratio.

00:00:33.926 --> 00:00:36.494
Crucially, it is split by RNA family,

00:00:36.574 --> 00:00:40.073
so no family appears in both training and testing.

00:00:40.153 --> 00:00:45.441
This homology-aware split, plus evaluation on the
external RPI2825 dataset,

00:00:45.521 --> 00:00:49.020
tests true generalization instead of memorization.
